 "title": "Who Are You? The Hardest Question",
 "topic": "mindset",
 "summary": "This video clip shows a scene where a man is asked the difficult question, \"Who are you?\" When he responds with his job title and hobbies, he is corrected because those describe what he does and his personality, not his core identity.",
 "key_points": [
  "Most people answer \"Who are you?\" by stating their job title or profession.",
  "Stating hobbies or personality traits describes what you do or like, not who you are.",
  "The question \"Who are you?\" is difficult for 99% of people to answer correctly."
 ],
 "content": "The video shows a clip featuring Jack Nicholson and Adam Sandler. Text on screen at the beginning reads \"The Question 99% of People Can't Answer\". Jack Nicholson asks, \"Tell us about yourself. Who are you?\". Adam Sandler responds, \"Well, I'm a... An executive assistant at a major pet products company, Dave.\". Jack Nicholson replies, \"I don't want you to tell us what you do. I want you to tell us who you are.\". Adam then tries again, saying, \"I'm a pretty good guy. I am... I like playing tennis on occasion.\". Jack Nicholson points out, \"Also, not your hobbies, Dave. Just simple. Tell us who you are.\". After some hesitation and laughter from the room, Adam tries once more: \"I'm a nice, easygoing man. I might be a little bit indecisive at times, Dave.\". Jack Nicholson corrects him again, saying, \"You're describing your personality. I want to know who you are.\". Adam finally gives up and says, \"I don't know what the hell you want me to say.\"",
